    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced. The bull case rests on verifiable technical strength \u2014 AAPL at 60-day highs with bullish MA alignment (price $195.03 > 10 EMA $191.52 > 200 SMA $179.59 > 50 SMA $177.70), a potential golden cross forming, and strong fundamentals ($62.6B operating cash flow, $61B shareholder returns). However, the bear's concerns are equally valid: MACD histogram has collapsed 97% (+1.67 to +0.04), RSI is overbought at 71.11, price is stretched 9.75% above the 50 SMA at the upper Bollinger Band, and volume at 1.04x average shows no fresh institutional accumulation. With no identifiable fundamental catalyst and the stock up 15% in 60 days, buying at the upper Bollinger Band is not a high-conviction entry, yet selling at 60-day highs with an intact uptrend would be fighting the tape. Maintaining existing exposure while avoiding aggressive new entries at $195 is the most defensible position.\n\n**Entry Price**: 191.52\n\n**Stop Loss**: 189.04\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-slightly-constructive weight (roughly benchmark weight). For new exposure, accumulate partial position at 10 EMA ($191.52) and add further at Bollinger middle ($189.04). Reassess thesis if price closes below $189.04.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
